  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nScattered showers and isolated to scattered thunderstorms will \ncontinue Saturday as another shortwave passes over in the flow \naloft. With PWATS remaining around the 90th percentile (as the LREF \nmean sees it), the hazards mentioned in the short-term Friday will \nalso carry over into Saturday. A warming and drying trend will set \nin to start the coming week as ridging builds into the intermountain \nwest. Isolated afternoon showers and thunderstorms (10-20% \nchance) will persist across higher terrain into the start of the\nweek. By mid-week, A low approaching from the west will lead to\nincreasing precipitation chances and a cooling trend yet again.",
